   "title": "US Treasury interest rates.webp",
   "description": "US Treasury interest ratesand the Federa funds rate The Federal Reserve FOMC sets the Federal funds rate . When this rate is raised above the longer-term 10 and 30 year U.S. Treasuries , it creates an inverted yield curve in order to reduce inflation and demand . This also leads the job market to cool down and can cause unemployment to rise. Short-term Treasuries such as the 1, 3, and 6 month bonds closely follow the Federal funds rate, while longer-term Treasuries are more influenced by expectations of future inflation.",
